#
# Accepted CVEs for the Trivy image gate (.github/workflows/images.yml).
# Only CVEs that are (a) bundled in a third-party base/runtime we cannot patch without a major
# upgrade AND (b) not reachable with attacker-controlled input in our deployment belong here.
# Each entry must carry a justification and an expiry so it is revisited.

# --- Apache Spark 4.1.2 bundled JARs (services/spark_jobs/*) ---
# These live in the Spark distribution's jars/ dir, not our code. Remediation is a Spark
# version upgrade, tracked as its own task (docs/operations/production-readiness.md). Spark 4.1
# already carries fixed avro and zookeeper, so the 3.5-era CVE-2024-47561 (avro) and
# CVE-2023-44981 (zookeeper) are gone; only Derby remains — and Derby is unused in our pipeline,
# so it is not reachable. (The image's OS packages are patched via `apt-get upgrade` at build, so
# base-layer CVEs like the linux-libc-dev kernel headers are fixed, not ignored. That sentence is a
# claim about a layer that is cached, and it was briefly false: with no changing input the upgrade
# was replayed from cache and the patch level froze, so the gate began failing on kernel-header CVEs
# this file promises are already fixed. The build now passes the patch layer a dated cache epoch —
# see SECURITY_REFRESH in .github/workflows/images.yml. Nothing about that belongs in this file; the
# point is that the claim above is only true for as long as that stays wired.)
CVE-2022-46337 exp:2026-09-30  # org.apache.derby:derby 10.16.1.1 — LDAP injection (Spark-bundled, Derby unused)
